# Files that run on the Raspberry Pi keep LF line endings, whatever the checkout's
# platform. Git for Windows converts to CRLF by default (core.autocrlf=true), and a copy
# made from such a checkout — WinSCP, FileZilla, a USB stick — then fails on the Pi with
# "$'\r': command not found" or "set: pipefail: invalid option".
*.sh       text eol=lf
*.service  text eol=lf
*.sudoers  text eol=lf
*.yaml     text eol=lf
*.yml      text eol=lf
